1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,254
The map had taught them to measure a gate in a minute; it had not taught them how to be at home.

2
00:00:05,254 --> 00:00:12,748
The third arc opened at home, in a kitchen with a fridge that hummed like a small, unhappy mule.

3
00:00:12,748 --> 00:00:20,751
Lin's mother was a textile worker, a daughter of farmers, and the mother of a boy who was never at home.

4
00:00:20,751 --> 00:00:24,421
“You reckon you are busy,” she said.

5
00:00:24,421 --> 00:00:27,565
“Ensure that you eat.”

6
00:00:27,565 --> 00:00:35,714
His grandson — his sister's boy — was doing a biographical project on an actress nobody in the family had heard of.

7
00:00:35,714 --> 00:00:50,531
The early pages would reveal a bad scare, a disastrous first draft, and the name of a granddaughter; three notebooks do not constitute a biography, and she said so whilst stirring the soup.

8
00:00:50,531 --> 00:01:03,019
“It is a thorough piece of work,” the boy said, “and it is a disaster.” A donkey brayed in a field, and a deer and a lioness were on the poster above the sink.

9
00:01:03,019 --> 00:01:10,537
“A tigress is not a house cat,” said the grandmother, “and neither is a daughter.”

10
00:01:10,537 --> 00:01:20,475
A suspicious neighbour, a scary story about a shaver left plugged in, and a horrible smell from the drain made the evening eventful.

11
00:01:20,475 --> 00:01:24,879
“Do not behave like a hero,” his mother said.

12
00:01:24,879 --> 00:01:38,557
“Negotiate.” The Olympic flag on the wall, faded by the sun, was the only decoration in the room, and the whole evening seemed to revolve around the cooker.

13
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:46,271
They talked about the baby boom, a baby boomer aunt, and a cock that crowed at four in the morning.

14
00:01:46,271 --> 00:01:58,944
“Humanity is not a measurable thing,” she said, “and that is the pity of it.” The doom of the small project was written into the timetable, and they both knew it.

15
00:01:58,944 --> 00:02:06,048
Any talk of plans was tragically short, and joyous only at the edges.

16
00:02:06,048 --> 00:02:17,950
What astonished him was the rhythm of the household: a rhythmic clatter, a humorous remark, a bowl of white rice, and a lot of unspoken resentment.

17
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:24,999
“Yes, sir,” the boy said, when his grandfather asked whether he would help.

18
00:02:24,999 --> 00:02:42,256
“I would tell you to centralize your work,” his mother said, “but your father could not do it either.” The best teacher he ever had was a kid of nine, later a neighbour, who knew the difference between a mean remark and a pound of rice.

19
00:02:42,256 --> 00:02:54,380
He could not amaze her with a plan; he could only turn up, particularly on the bad days, and that was the increase she had asked for.
